===Etymology===
[[Image:Pahoehoe toe.jpg|thumb|250px|Lava]]
{{dercat|en|qfa-sub}}
From {{bor|en|it|-}}, from {{der|en|nap,scn|lava|t=lava; downpour overflowing the streets}}, likely from {{der|en|la|lābēs|t=a fall; a collapse; subsidence}}; compare {{m|la|lābīna|t=landslide}}. A supposed relation with {{m|la|lavo|lavare|t=to wash}} is now widely discredited, nor is there probably any relation with {{noncog|ar|لابة|t=black volcanic rock}}. {{rfv-etym|en}} Alternatively, the Romance words are connected with {{cog|oc-pro|lavo}}, {{m|oc-pro|lauvo|t=flat stone}}, from a {{der|en|la-vul|-}} source borrowed from a {{der|en|cel}} language such as {{der|en|cel-gau|*lawā}},<ref>{{R:cel:EDPC|242|head=*līwank-}}</ref> but ultimately of obscure origin; see {{der|en|cel-pro|*līwos|id=stone}} for details.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|läʹvə|a=RP,US,AU,NZ}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈlɑːvə/|a=RP}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈlɑvə/|a=US}}
*** {{audio|en|en-us-lava.ogg|a=US}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈlɐːvə/|a=AU,NZ}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɑvə/|/ˈlævə/|a=CA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlavə/|a=Scotland}}
* {{homophones|en|larva<aa:non-rhotic>|lather<aa:non-rhotic,th-fronting,trap-bath split>}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːvə|ævə|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[molten]] [[rock]] ejected by a [[volcano]] from a vent such as a [[crater]] or [[fissure]]; [[magma]] that has breached the surface of the earth.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author={{w|Martha Holmes (broadcaster)|Martha Holmes}}|title=Sea Trek|publisher=BBC Books|page=44
|passage=Marine iguanas line the shores of the islands, and are usually seen sprawled over '''lava''' rocks near the sea.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A body of lava.
# {{lb|en|dated}} Solidified lava.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1896|author={{w|H.G. Wells}}|title=The Island of Dr. Moreau|publisher=Stone & Kimball|page=48
|passage=I leant forward to see him better, and a piece of '''lava''', detached by my hand, went pattering down the slope.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|proscribed}} {{U|magma}}.<!--, molten rock ''within'' the earth-->
# A shade of red, named after the volcanic lava.
#: {{color panel|CF1020}}
# {{rfv-sense|en}} {{lb|en|figuratively|colloquial}} [[hot|Hot]] [[water]].

====Usage notes====
