|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/books-and-arts/21606252-ideal-political-role-model-freedom-fighter Freedom fighter]
|passage=[Edmund] Burke continued to fight for '''liberty''' later on in life. He backed Americans in their campaign for freedom from British taxation. He supported Catholic freedoms and freer trade with Ireland, in spite of his constituents’ ire. He wanted more liberal laws on the punishment of debtors.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021-03-07|author=Ross Douthat|title=Do Liberals Care if Books Disappear?|newspaper=w:The New York Times| titleurl=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/06/opinion/dr-seuss-books-liberalism.html|text=Now liberal cultural power has increased, the ACLU doesn’t seem very interested in the '''liberties''' of non-progressives anymore, and Dr. Seuss sells as pricey samizdat.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251029074334/https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/06/opinion/dr-seuss-books-liberalism.html|archivedate=29 October 2025}}
# The condition of being free from [[imprisonment]], [[slavery]] or [[force]]d [[labour]].
#: {{ux|en|The prisoners gained their '''liberty''' from an underground tunnel.}}
# The condition of being free to [[act]], [[believe]] or [[express]] [[oneself]] as one [[choose]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Everyone has the right to life, '''liberty''' and security of person.}}
#* {{RQ:Burns Poems|volume=III|poem=The Tree of Liberty|page=360|passage=I'd gie my ſhoon frae aff my feet, / To taſte ſic fruit, I ſwear, man. / Syne let us pray, auld England may / Sure plant this far-famed tree, man; / And blythe we'll ſing, and hail the day / That gave us '''liberty''', man.}}
# [[freedom|Freedom]] from [[excess]]ive [[government]] control.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2012-12-14|author=w:Simon Jenkins|volume=188|issue=2|page=23|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/commentisfree/2012/dec/14/north-korea-boys-toys-threat-reaction We mustn't overreact to North Korea boys' toys]
|passage=The threat of terrorism to the British lies in the overreaction to it of British governments. Each one in turn clicks up the ratchet of surveillance, intrusion and security. Each one diminishes '''liberty'''.}}
# A short [[period]] when a [[sailor]] is allowed [[ashore]].
#: {{ux|en|We're going on a three-day '''liberty''' as soon as we dock.}}
